# Per-session state left by the session gate this repository retired, and
# worktrees created by agents. The harness hooks in `.claude/hooks/` keep no
# state at all: each one reads the tree in front of it and writes nothing.
.claude/state/
.claude/worktrees/

# What the Cloudflare CLI caches when somebody runs `wrangler` in this
# repository, which holds an account identifier and nothing this project
# authored. `wrangler.jsonc` beside it is committed, because it names the
# directory the deploy serves and a reviewer reads that.
.wrangler/

# The check cache. The lock beside it is committed, because a reviewer reads
# the taxonomy a verdict came from. This one holds no fact of its own: every
# entry is recomputable from the tree it was written over, and a run that finds
# none is slower and never different.
.headwater/cache/

# What `mkdocs build` writes, per `mkdocs.yml`. It is the rendered projection of
# the corpus and every byte of it is recomputable from the tree beside it, so
# nothing is lost by leaving it out. It is deliberately not the MkDocs default
# of `site/`, which is the hand-built half HW-DR-0037 governs and which is
# committed byte for byte.
.headwater/site-build/

# What `tools/site/assemble-site.sh` composes from the two halves above, and what the
# deploy serves. Every byte of it is a copy of a byte that is either committed
# under `site/` or recomputable into `.headwater/site-build/`, so it holds
# nothing of its own. HW-DR-0047 rules that this is the served directory.
.headwater/site-deploy/

__pycache__/
